            {
              "id": "cmrurczw400az3d7bhcphr1xu",
              "heading": "<strong>Heading</strong>",
              "paragraph": "<div data-editor-id=\"51b67ce6-f745-492d-a942-6794a2ae7527\"><p>This final video reviews the key lessons from the course and reinforces that effective engagement depends on clear goals, thoughtful design, human judgment, and a commitment to act on what communities contribute. It introduces additional resources, including an AI-powered coaching tool, to help learners design their own engagement projects.</p></div>"
            }
          ],
          "family": "text",
          "variant": "paragraph",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:37:54.542Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-07-21T14:37:54.542Z",
          "globalBlockId": "5b3c164e-29a1-40d9-8cad-5daf6342c581"
        },
        {
          "id": "ebzuxFXZkf66AkrFVxJiQwHrSHKohlLA",
          "settings": {
            "v": 2,
            "paddingTop": 3,
            "zoomOnClick": true,
            "quotesInline": false,
            "audioPosition": "bottom",
            "paddingBottom": 3,
            "paddingLinked": true,
            "markerColorContrast": "AUTO",
            "snippetColorContrast": "AUTO"
          },
          "type": "interactive",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "cmry5j1gu003r3d7djfn2awxs",
              "title": "Audio Description Transcript: Video 12",
              "description": "<div data-editor-id=\"481e2e99-a404-4fda-8f5d-c8e63071e227\"><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: The InnovateUS Logo appears.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: Title appears: Designing Democratic Engagement with AI: Practical Strategies for Public Participation.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: Title appears: Conclusion.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">This course began with a simple observation.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: Text appears with the speaker: Beth Simone Noveck, Professor, Northeastern University.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">As public professionals, we want to engage our communities, but would benefit from more guidance about how to do so effectively. The course you've completed is designed to close that gap.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">Together, we've walked through nine steps for designing effective engagement with communities.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: Bullet points appear: Defining goals for engagement and action. Ensuring ownership, accountability and action. Identifying participants. Designing outreach strategies. Designing incentives for participation. Designing the tasks: what you ask participants to do. Reviewing inputs. Using what the group creates.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">We've also seen how governments and organizations around the world are putting these ideas into practice.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: Text appears with the speaker: Danielle Allen, Professor, Harvard University.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">Along the way, we explored how you can use AI to support each step, helping you work more efficiently and effectively. But the foundation remains the same: clear goals, thoughtful design, human judgment, and a commitment to act on what communities contribute.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">The next step is to put these ideas into practice. This course is a starting point. If you want to go deeper, we offer additional workshops and resources, including an AI-powered coaching tool to help you design your own engagement project step by step.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">[Visual description]: The InnovateUS website is shown on the Coach page. An AI tool asking the following question: What public engagement challenge are you working on today? There is a text submission box to answer and ask questions.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">Public engagement is not easy. It requires time, effort, and a willingness to listen. But when done well, it leads to better decisions, stronger trust, and communities who know that their voices matter.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\">Thank you for taking part.</p><p style=\"line-height: 1.5\"><br class=\"break-when-trailing\"></p></div>"
            }
          ],
